{"name":"Hibiscus","hex":"#b6316c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Hibiscus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Malvaceae – hibiscuses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Hibiscus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hibiscus","blocks":[{"text":"Hibiscus is a genus of plants in the family Malvaceae native to the tropics and subtropics. The genus is quite large, comprising 319 species. Hibiscus are renowned for their large, showy flowers and those species are commonly known simply as \"hibiscus\", or less widely known as rose mallow. The genus includes both annual and perennial herbaceous plants, as well as woody shrubs and small trees."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Hibiscus_flower_TZ.jpg/330px-Hibiscus_flower_TZ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hibiscus","wikidata":"Q157124"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg/500px-Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg/1280px-Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg/500px-Fou_-_sea_hibiscus_%28Hibiscus_tiliaceus%29_flower_and_leaf_%28Niue%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hibiscus tiliaceus in flower","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFou_-_sea_hibiscus_(Hibiscus_tiliaceus)_flower